  Divergences that survived refutation:
  [{"requirement":{"id":"REQ-23","quote":"No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade.","location":"DESIGN.md line 2, sentence 9 (administrator)","kind":"access-control","force":"mandatory","checkable":"No account (deployer, sponsor, treasury or other) has privileged control over the factory or raffles: no owner/role, pause, cancel, rescue, parameter setter or forced withdrawal.","document":"DESIGN.md"},"alignment":{"requirementId":"REQ-23","verdict":"contradicted","confidence":"high","analysisFile":"/Users/hishamel-husseini/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/21/01a15d64-4430-7440-b259-192acf9762b5/raffle-audit-r001-claude/cells/CLAUDE-TOB/S5/attempt-03/work/spec-compliance/requirements/02-REQ-23.md","reasoning":"Raffle.sol:L282 exempts the sponsor from the endTime gate on the empty-raffle branch of enableRefunds. While the raffle is Active with zero entries, only the sponsor can end it before endTime. L299 sets Refunding, which is terminal: no status writer accepts Refunding as a starting state. Anyone can then call releaseSponsorPrize (L395-L407), which returns the prize to sponsorRecipient. Every raffle is Active with zero entries from the moment createRaffle returns, so this cancel power exists on every raffle until its first sale.

The test names both 'sponsor' and 'cancel', and the code grants that power deliberately. This is an affirmative grant, not a check missing on one path, so the verdict is contradicted rather than partial. NatSpec also documents it as an 'empty-raffle cancellation authority'.

Every other clause holds:
- Factory config is immutable (RaffleFactory.sol L33-L42) and written only in the constructor.
- Clone config is written only in initialize (Raffle.sol L197-L204), which runs once (L177/L179) and only for the factory (L178).
- Economic values are constants.
- Clones use ERC-1167 bytecode with the implementation address fixed in code (Clones.sol L54-L57).
- There is no delegatecall, selfdestruct, sstore or create2 in src.
- Every caller check is either a bearer check DESIGN.md asks for, the trusted wrapper callback, or the one-time creation gate.
- No asset movement takes a destination, token or amount chosen by a privileged account.
- Neither the deployer nor the treasury holds a role.

