ent is a contract that records NFTs only in onERC721Received (a vault or pool), or one that cannot move ERC-721s at all (a USDC splitter). Any stranger can push the NFT into it unrecorded or unrecoverable, and the claim flag blocks any second attempt. A safe transfer would have reverted and left the prize in escrow. Impact is limited to contract recipients, so severity is low. A narrow corollary: sponsorRecipient is checked against the raffle registry only at creation (RaffleFactory.sol:166), and only if it already has code (Raffle.sol:602). Clones are deployed with CREATE (packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol:57), so their addresses are predictable. If a sponsor names a future clone address as recipient, releaseSponsorProceeds later reverts with InvalidQuoteDestination (Raffle.sol:565), but releaseSponsorPrize still moves the NFT into that other clone. That contradicts DESIGN.md "Never move assets between raffle clones." This requires the sponsor's own misconfiguration and harms only the sponsor."}]

